13. Argo CD GitHub Repository Configuration
13.1 Repository Secret
Example file: repo-secret.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: zomato-github-repo
  namespace: argocd
  labels:
    argocd.argoproj.io/secret-type: repository
stringData:
  type: git
  url: https://github.com/psreddy2508/DevOps-Project-Zomato-Kastro.git
Apply:
kubectl apply -f repo-secret.yaml
(Registers the GitHub repository with Argo CD. This is the public repository used for our project.)
13.2 Argo CD Application manifest
Example file: zomato-app.yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: zomato
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/psreddy2508/DevOps-Project-Zomato-Kastro.git
    targetRevision: master
    path: Kubernetes
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: default
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
      - CreateNamespace=true
Apply:
kubectl apply -f zomato-app.yaml
(Creates the Argo CD Application. It watches the master branch and the Kubernetes directory in GitHub.)
13.3 Correct the Git branch
kubectl patch application zomato -n argocd \
  --type merge \
  -p '{"spec":{"source":{"targetRevision":"master"}}}'
(Changes the Argo CD target revision from main to master. We used this because the actual GitHub branch was master.)
13.4 Refresh the application
kubectl annotate application zomato -n argocd \
  argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite
(Forces Argo CD to refresh repository information and compare the Git source with the live cluster.)
13.5 Check synchronization status
kubectl get applications -n argocd
(Displays application sync and health status.)
kubectl describe application zomato -n argocd
(Displays detailed sync status, Git revision, resources, events and errors.)
14. Zomato Application Deployment
The repository contains:
Kubernetes/
├── deployment.yaml
└── service.yaml
We removed node-service.yaml because it was an unrelated monitoring Service referencing a missing namespace.
14.1 Deployment manifest
File: Kubernetes/deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: zomato
  labels:
    app: zomato
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: zomato
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: zomato
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: zomato
        image: kastrov/zomato:latest
        ports:
        - containerPort: 3000
(Deploys two Zomato application replicas using the Docker image kastrov/zomato:latest. The container is configured for port 3000.)
14.2 Service manifest
File: Kubernetes/service.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: zomato
  labels:
    app: zomato
spec:
  type: NodePort
  ports:
  - port: 3000
    targetPort: 3000
    nodePort: 30001
  selector:
    app: zomato
(Creates a NodePort Service. It listens on port 30001 on each node and forwards requests to application pods on port 3000.)
15. Zomato Application Verification
15.1 Check pods
kubectl get pods -n default -o wide
(Displays Zomato pods, readiness, status, restarts, pod IP and node placement.)
15.2 Check Deployment
kubectl get deployment zomato -n default
(Checks desired, current and available replicas.)
15.3 Check Service
kubectl get svc zomato -n default
(Checks Service type, ClusterIP and NodePort.)
15.4 Describe Deployment
kubectl describe deployment zomato -n default
(Displays deployment details, replica status and related events.)
15.5 Check application logs
kubectl logs deployment/zomato -n default --tail=50
(Displays the latest 50 log lines from a selected Zomato pod.)
15.6 Check Service endpoints
kubectl get endpoints zomato -n default
(Checks which pod IP addresses are registered as backend endpoints for the Zomato Service.)
15.7 Test NodePort
curl -I http://127.0.0.1:30001
(Tests HTTP connectivity to the NodePort from the node. The HTTP response depends on application behavior.)
15.8 Open the application
http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:30001
(Opens Zomato from a browser. Allow inbound TCP port 30001 in the EC2 Security Group, preferably only from your public IP.)
